    {
      "v": 18,
      "zh": "于是国民都到巴力庙，拆毁了庙，打碎坛和像，又在坛前将巴力的祭司玛坦杀了。祭司耶何耶大派官看守耶和华的殿，",
      "en": "All the people of the land went and demolished[NOTE:1] the temple of Baal. They smashed its altars and idols[NOTE:2] to bits.[NOTE:3] They killed Mattan the priest of Baal in front of the altar. Jehoiada the priest[NOTE:4] then placed guards at the Lord’s temple.",
      "notes": [
        "Or “tore down.”",
        "Or “images.”",
        "The Hebrew construction translated “smashed…to bits” is emphatic. The adverbial infinitive absolute (הֵיטֵב [hetev], “well”) accompanying the Piel form of the verb שָׁבַר (shavar), “break,” suggests thorough demolition.",
        "Heb “the priest.” Jehoiada’s name is added for clarification."
